# The build context is the repository's root (docker build -f apps/imgserver/Dockerfile .). BuildKit
# reads this file, named after the Dockerfile, in place of a .dockerignore: everything is denied,
# then what the server needs is allowed: the library's package, the server's modules and its lock.
# No tests, no tools, no research, no upstream submodules, no environment or cache.
*

!core/pyproject.toml
!core/LICENSE
!core/NOTICE
!core/seedvr2x

!apps/imgserver/pyproject.toml
!apps/imgserver/uv.lock
!apps/imgserver/.python-version
!apps/imgserver/LICENSE
!apps/imgserver/NOTICE
!apps/imgserver/README.md
!apps/imgserver/*.py

**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
